1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,475
This woman was so shameless, she told
investors her company made a hundred
million dollars.

2
00:00:05,675 --> 00:00:07,156
It made a hundred thousand.

3
00:00:07,606 --> 00:00:13,954
Theranos.  Elizabeth Holmes promised blood
tests from a single finger prick, on a
machine called Edison.

4
00:00:14,254 --> 00:00:17,774
Investors poured in over seven hundred
million dollars.

5
00:00:17,774 --> 00:00:19,631
The valuation?  Nine billion.

6
00:00:19,631 --> 00:00:24,175
Forbes called her the youngest self-made
female billionaire in America.

7
00:00:24,475 --> 00:00:26,361
Hit like if you'd have invested too.

8
00:00:26,661 --> 00:00:35,565
The problem?  The Wall Street Journal
reported the Edison gave inaccurate
results, and the company ran its tests on
ordinary commercial machines.

9
00:00:35,865 --> 00:00:39,102
Send this to the friend who believes every
startup pitch.

10
00:00:39,402 --> 00:00:42,556
Then Theranos voided two years of Edison
results.

11
00:00:42,906 --> 00:00:45,739
Follow along. The number always gives them
away.

12
00:00:46,039 --> 00:00:49,963
Guilty on four counts. Eleven years and
three months in prison.

13
00:00:50,413 --> 00:00:53,483
A hundred million, claimed. A hundred
thousand, real.
